<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://www.semanticweb.org/y6g/ontologies/2025/FDD_ON_VAV_HVAC/"
     xml:base="http://www.semanticweb.org/y6g/ontologies/2025/FDD_ON_VAV_HVAC/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:FDD_ON_VAV_HVAC="http://www.semanticweb.org/y6g/ontologies/2025/FDD_ON_VAV_HVAC#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/y6g/ontologies/2025/FDD_ON_VAV_HVAC">
        <rdfs:comment>1. Copyright and version control
Copyright
The development of FDD-ON is led by Dr. Yimin Chen.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>2. Brief introduction
FDD Ontology for VAV HVAC systems (FDD-ON_VAV_HVAC) is an sub ontology of FDD-ON, which is an ontology of fault detection and diagnostics (FDD) for heating, ventilation, air conditioning and refrigeration (HVAC&amp;R) systems. This part of the ontology is for Variable Air Volume (VAV) HVAC systems.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="gmail.com">3. Maintenance and evoluation 
FDD-ON will evolve by adding  types of systems, equipment, components, as well as expanding the libraries for faults, symptoms, and impacts correspondingly.

We welcome the community contributes the evoluation of FDD-ON.

Please direct all comments and questions to chenyimincareer</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>4. Version control
1) The version of libraries is 2026B (released on July 20, 2026).
2) The version of controlled vocabulary lists is 2026A (relased on January 25, 2026).
3) The version of taxonomies is 2025B (was released on  December 1, 2025).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


